#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054275 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f986c29-111e-5cb3-8104-62ab734f1c47" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of an Indexed Family"}] :question/id #uuid "154d4cf7-a72a-51b1-bbb3-9bcf83b88e98" :question/math-academy-id "e-12665" :question/problem "Find $T_2$ given that $T_n = \\{ 1, 2, \\ldots, 2n+1 \\},$ where $n \\in \\mathbb{N}.$" :question/worked-solution "To write down the elements of $T_2,$ we substitute $n=2$ into the expression and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{2} & ={1,2,…,2(2)+1} \\\\  & ={1,2,…,5} \\\\  & ={1,2,3,4,5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054282 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "957a2f61-61b1-5675-ba84-5348a47af986" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unions and Intersections of Finite Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "60e24dac-c47a-53ee-9c91-0e6987e966f0" :question/math-academy-id "e-12763" :question/problem "Find $\\,\\displaystyle \\bigcup_{i \\in I} S_i$, given that $I = \\{ -1, 0, 1 \\},$ and $S_i = (i-1, \\,i+1).$" :question/worked-solution "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n\\bigcup_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{ x\\in U \\: : \\: x \\in A_i \\:\\:\\textrm{for at least one } A_i,\\:\\: i \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1} \\\\  & =(-2,0)\\,\\cup \\,(-1,1)\\,\\cup \\,(0,2) \\\\  & =(-2,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054283 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1e93acb-6c0b-5263-9df9-9dcc00680845" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unions and Intersections of (Countably) Infinite Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "842ee2c1-8e78-56dd-b109-b9fcc273704e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12764" :question/problem "Find $\\,\\displaystyle \\bigcap_{i \\in I} X_i$  given that $I = \\mathbb{N}$ and $X_i = \\{ i, \\, 2i \\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The intersection of a family of indexed sets $\\{A_i\\}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n\\bigcap_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{ x\\in U \\: : \\: x \\in A_i \\:\\:\\textrm{for all } A_i,\\:\\: i \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have $X_1 = \\{ 1, 2 \\}$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have $X_2 = \\{ 2, 4 \\}$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have $X_3 = \\{ 3, 6 \\}$\n\n- if $i=4,$ we have $X_4 = \\{ 4, 8 \\}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f986c29-111e-5cb3-8104-62ab734f1c47" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of an Indexed Family"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a41d844b-a17d-5f56-b2ac-5ef53397a937" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-2,-1, 0, 1, 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051696} {:answer/id #uuid "c607dee7-292f-56d4-857f-69c669c1f240" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-4, 0, 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051697} {:answer/id #uuid "f71e639e-aa99-5e93-9025-736c54785389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-2, 0, 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051698} {:answer/id #uuid "35921484-5768-5484-8ebb-9a8a12f489c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051699} {:answer/id #uuid "47807ad2-a124-5b85-af75-4b2c042e37b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-4,-3,-2,-1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c607dee7-292f-56d4-857f-69c669c1f240" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{